{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1066287-after-the-time-of-judgement","id":1066287,"title":"After \"The Time of Judgement\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-22T07:10:19-07:00","id":1066287,"title":"After \"The Time of Judgement\"","content":"Considering the fact that the books on the &quot;end of the world&quot; have already been printed and the world of darkness books mean to continue on regardless, I and some friends thought it'd be a little weird to go back to the &quot;everything is going to end&quot; theme. So we've been trying to think of a setting &quot;after the end that didn't end&quot;, but keeping with the old themes. We'd like some thoughts.<br /> <br /> For a baseline, We wanted to go for &quot;the big fight came and everyone lost&quot;, the good guys banding together with all their resources to take on the bad guys only to loose, and for it not to matter because the bad guy's plans didn't go how they expected. here are the cliff notes:<br /> <br /> To start off with we have werewolf's &quot;war across the umbra&quot;. The wyrms minions had begun to awaken and summon the wyrm via reality anchors across the globe(apart from the TOJ books they needed an anchor for each urges wyrm and elemental wyrm as well. If the werewolves stopped them from getting one they need ed to find another). The torment the wyrm had been causing the world had been revealed for the purpose of creating and feeding an army of banes that it had now released into the middle umbra in force. Split between stopping the wyrm ritual and defending the umbra the werewolves realized they were seriously undermanned, choosing to send emissaries to try and rally the septs and fera to finally drop their centuries long hatred for the final battle in gaia's name. (Insert epic campaign with your favorite parts from WTA: The Apocalypse here). After a full blown spirit war in the umbra and a combination game of hide and seek/chess on earth: The fera take back the umbra, but fail to prevent the kidnapping of the final anchor. (Gaian army marching forward to stop Big ritual in an umbran stronghold on malpheas). The wyrm breaks free of it's prison and... devours it's own incarnae. The wyrm is now the sole power in malpheas and is content to use it's power to indirectly turn the world into a living hell to farm for infinite misery rather than consume it and run out of things to eat. The garou return in shame and anger, pointing fingers over why they lost, and arguing over there place now that the wyrm is free. All on edge as they consider what they should/can do to pretect the world from now on.<br /> <br /> Second, &quot;vampire&quot; and &quot;demon&quot; games are assumed to both exist and acknowledge each other in the same setting.(vampire perspective) The sudden spike in infernalism and demon cults across the world has alerted the camerilla. Elders are on edge about loosing some of there power base as former puppets become immune to their mind altering powers. The sabbat is already going mental about signs of gehenna(as always), but have started a troubling campaign of killing killing former known pawns, people of high standing, and some random individuals they claim to be &quot;demons&quot;. Their activities are putting to much strain on the masquerade, and the ventrue are left speculating if the lambrosa have finally lost their grip on their pet lunatics.(Demon perspective) After being thrown into the world and quickly establishing themselves, the factions have begun hitting their first roadblocks many of the individuals in power they have tried to sway have acted uncharacteristic of humans when offered the pact. Acting with an obsessive love or loyalty toward a a dark master or mistress of theirs, many had to be coaxed indirectly or by altering their minds. Often the power of the pact was needed to shield them from control only to leave them with fuzzy ideas of people they never met or missing memories. Other times the person was too unshakable and needed to be slain before such powerful masters could be warned. Many known faustians, lucifarians, or even raveners are being found dead or hidden away in the nearest vessel they could find often speaking of savage monsters, monstrosities of flesh, or the living shadows from the abyss itself coming upon them in the night to rend their host bodies. The highest courts wonder what machinations of demon or earthbound could be causing this, but many cryptics have been sending warnings of the &quot;Children of Caine&quot;....(cue game of noir style investigation and game of thrones politics. with weaker but more numerous ghouls and stronger/quickly growing numbers of thralls offing each other in the &quot;War of Shadows&quot;. ending and how the &quot;withering&quot; fits in is still unknown. Note: the only reason the sabbat would recognize the demons first is because of the black hand and talmahera's background in infernalism. They'd recognize the demons for what they are and immediately point the sabbat at them like a shotgun.)<br /> <br /> For mage this would be the end of the avatar storm when the masters/control re-established contact after desperately preserving horizon/the ivory tower and discovering the nephandi masters had used this time to establish a power base, gather resources, and prepare for the great decent while their students and adepts ran around blind on earth. They individually attempted to take down the demon and nephandi infested &quot;Hive&quot; nodes one-by-one only to realize the important ones are to deep to find or attack without more members. Traditions and techies band together (magical and scientific vs demon war begins). (Big reveal that the nephandi have collected enough power and members to change the course of an astroid to hit earth, and are using the nihilism of the world to open a spiritual black hole in the umbra).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:06:33-07:00","id":1066511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1066287-after-the-time-of-judgement#post1066287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To start off with we have werewolf's &quot;war across the umbra&quot;. The wyrms minions had begun to awaken and summon the wyrm via reality anchors across the globe(apart from the TOJ books they needed an anchor for each urges wyrm and elemental wyrm as well. If the werewolves stopped them from getting one they need ed to find another). The torment the wyrm had been causing the world had been revealed for the purpose of creating and feeding an army of banes that it had now released into the middle umbra in force. Split between stopping the wyrm ritual and defending the umbra the werewolves realized they were seriously undermanned, choosing to send emissaries to try and rally the septs and fera to finally drop their centuries long hatred for the final battle in gaia's name. (Insert epic campaign with your favorite parts from WTA: The Apocalypse here). After a full blown spirit war in the umbra and a combination game of hide and seek/chess on earth: The fera take back the umbra, but fail to prevent the kidnapping of the final anchor. (Gaian army marching forward to stop Big ritual in an umbran stronghold on malpheas). The wyrm breaks free of it's prison and... devours it's own incarnae. The wyrm is now the sole power in malpheas and is content to use it's power to indirectly turn the world into a living hell to farm for infinite misery rather than consume it and run out of things to eat. The garou return in shame and anger, pointing fingers over why they lost, and arguing over there place now that the wyrm is free. All on edge as they consider what they should/can do to pretect the world from now on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd advise you to dial back what got freed, because the Wyrm being freed is the Good End of Weaver Ascendant, in that the Wyrm, when free to do its job, does not turn things into a living hell. The ones responsible for this were the little bits and pieces of it that found that they liked shitting everything up, as it gave them power and authority over an increasingly wide range of territory. Also as detailed in the WA scenario, it means changes that are so drastic that you basically aren't playing anything resembling what the old games were. So, go with Triatic Wyrms having free rein, or perhaps just more Maeljin manifestations across the world, because freeing up Supernals to do what they actually should be doing is not going to result in the same Apocalypse outcome that you're describing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:12:06-07:00","id":1066889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1066287-after-the-time-of-judgement?p=1066511#post1066511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd advise you to dial back what got freed, because the Wyrm being freed is the Good End of Weaver Ascendant, in that the Wyrm, when free to do its job, does not turn things into a living hell. The ones responsible for this were the little bits and pieces of it that found that they liked shitting everything up, as it gave them power and authority over an increasingly wide range of territory. Also as detailed in the WA scenario, it means changes that are so drastic that you basically aren't playing anything resembling what the old games were. So, go with Triatic Wyrms having free rein, or perhaps just more Maeljin manifestations across the world, because freeing up Supernals to do what they actually should be doing is not going to result in the same Apocalypse outcome that you're describing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we were sort of subscribing to the idea that the wyrm did go insane after it got trapped. Which I think is supported by many of the other senarios in the apocalypse book, after all they were all completely different takes on the universe in many ways. For example: the last battleground senario that we based ours of, the triatic wyrm can be interpreted to be the wyrm(or what's left of it) and malpheas itself being the prison that was built for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T17:36:20-07:00","id":1067861,"title":"","content":"For Vampire I really like the optional end posed at the end of <i>The Crucible of God</i>, where the players become the new... well, they are not from before the flood. What would the equivalent be of &quot;before the disaster&quot; or &quot;before the apocalypse&quot;? Boost their power but not by too much, set a new baseline for these new &quot;second generation&quot; of vampires and continue from there. For Demon I'd go with <i>Paradise Won</i>; Lucifer wins and sees that not all of the Fallen are Earthbound material. But the world is in tatters and it needs rebuilding.<br /> <br /> There could be a bit of a crossover even. Monsters born from the war and Tzimisce's rampant powers has left things out there that need to be fought. The new angels fight in the light while vampires fight in the dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}